;;
;;;; Scope resolution (K: scope-resolution.k)
;;
;; self/parent resolution ($classref_to_id, pulled forward to 4.09 since
;; 4.10's method-call rules need it too), static method call (surface rules
;; are in 4.10, next to the ordinary method-call machinery they share), class
;; constants and static properties.
;;

;;
;;;; Access to class static properties (K: 'ScopeResolution on a $prop)
;;

;;; a static property lives in the class's static-scope array — walking up
;;; through the parent chain the same way class constants do below (kphp's
;;; parser only reaches SPROP at the class where it is declared, but the
;;; lookup itself is not restricted to it; ported for the general case)
rule Step/sprop:
  `< ((SPROP classRef id_prop) :: kitem*) `; config > ~>
  `< ((REF loc (STR id_prop)) :: kitem*) `; config >
  -- if id_cls = $classref_to_id(config.CTRL.CLS, config.CLASSES, classRef)
  -- if classDef = $find_map<id, classDef>(config.CLASSES, id_cls)
  -- if loc = classDef.STATICS

;;
;;;; Class constants (K: 'ClassConstant)
;;
;; kphp's class constants are not supported (classes.k traps
;; ClassConstantDeclList at declaration), so CLSCONST is unreachable through
;; any class actually declared by this semantics — kept stuck, as in K (no
;; class ever populates a constant entry in its static-scope array for a
;; genuine `const` declaration; 4.09's CONSTS case already traps the surface
;; declaration as NOT-SUPPORTED before any CLSCONST could observe it).
;;
